viated as GW) is a British miniature wargaming manufacturing company. Games Workshop is best known as developer and publisher of the tabletop wargames Warhammer Fantasy Battles,…</span>\n                </a>\n            \n        </div>\n        \n\n        <div class=\"topic-content\">\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Created By\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/warhammer-fantasy/games-workshop\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            Games Workshop\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>Games Workshop created Warhammer Fantasy.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </details>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"topic-section\">\n    <details>\n        <summary class=\"topic-summary\">\n            <span class=\"topic-title\">Published By</span>\n            <span class=\"topic-count\">1</span>\n        </summary>\n\n        \n\n        <div class=\"topic-content\">\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Published By\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/warhammer-fantasy/games-workshop\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            Games Workshop\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>Games Workshop publishes Warhammer Fantasy products.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </details>\n</section>\n\n</section>\n\n\n<section class=\"did-you-know\">\n    <h2>Did you know?</h2>\n    <ul>\n        <li>Warhammer Fantasy is also referenced as Warhammer Fantasy Battle, WHFB, Old World Warhammer.</li><li>Games Workshop created Warhammer Fantasy.</li><li>The Old World is the core Warhammer Fantasy setting.</li><li>Games Workshop publishes Warhammer Fantasy products.</li><li>The End Times concluded classic Warhammer Fantasy.</li><li>Evidence around Warhammer Fantasy is classified as fiction on Ton-o-Lore.</li>\n    </ul>\n</section>","overview":"<section class=\"overview\">\n    <h2>What is Warhammer Fantasy?</h2>\n    \n    <p>\n        Warhammer Fantasy Battle, often abbreviated by fans as WFB, WHFB, or simply Warhammer, is the oldest and most popular tabletop miniature war game to use Game Workshop&#039;s original Warhammer setting of the Known World. The game&#039;s 8th Edition, released in 2010, was its last, as the setting was brought to an end in the apocalypse of the End Times and was replaced by a new high fantasy setting known as Warhammer: Age of Sigmar in 2015.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        However, in 2024, <a href=\"/warhammer-fantasy/games-workshop\" class=\"entity-link\">Games Workshop</a> released Warhammer: <a href=\"/warhammer-fantasy/old-world\" class=\"entity-link\">The Old World</a>, a new iteration of the original tabletop game set in an earlier timeline in the 23rd century IC prior to the Great War Against Chaos.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        The game is set in a dark fantasy world much like our own called the &quot;Known World&quot; or the &quot;mortal world&quot; by its inhabitants. It is home to a vast number of magical and fantastical beasts and intelligent races, each with their own civilisations, customs, and enmities.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        Many are based on the traditional high fantasy races dating back to the works of J.R.R. Tolkien such as Men, Elves, Dwarfs, and Dragons, but many are also original, such as the Lizardmen, Skaven, and Ogres.\n    </p>\n    \n    <p class=\"also-known-as\">\n        <strong>Also known as:</strong>\n        Warhammer Fantasy Battle, WHFB, Old World Warhammer.\n    </p>\n\n</section>","word_count":903,"uniqueness_score":"1.0000"},"entity":{"id":"d31ddbed-a7b9-435c-b963-df3ae1eec46d","name":"Warhammer Fantasy","slug":"warhammer-fantasy","type":"topic","kind":"topic","type_label":"Topic","short_description":"Warhammer Fantasy Battle, often abbreviated by fans as WFB, WHFB, or simply Warhammer, is the oldest and most popular tabletop miniature war game to use Game Workshop's original Warhammer setting of the Known World. The…","description":"Warhammer Fantasy Battle, often abbreviated by fans as WFB, WHFB, or simply Warhammer, is the oldest and most popular tabletop miniature war game to use Game Workshop's original Warhammer setting of the Known World. The game's 8th Edition, released in 2010, was its last, as the setting was brought to an end in the apocalypse of the End Times and was replaced by a new high fantasy setting known as Warhammer: Age of Sigmar in 2015.\n\nHowever, in 2024, Games Workshop released Warhammer: The Old World, a new iteration of the original tabletop game set in an earlier timeline in the 23rd century IC prior to the Great War Against Chaos.\n\nThe game is set in a dark fantasy world much like our own called the \"Known World\" or the \"mortal world\" by its inhabitants. It is home to a vast number of magical and fantastical beasts and intelligent races, each with their own civilisations, customs, and enmities.\n\nMany are based on the traditional high fantasy races dating back to the works of J.R.R. Tolkien such as Men, Elves, Dwarfs, and Dragons, but many are also original, such as the Lizardmen, Skaven, and Ogres.","evidence":"fiction","universe":"warhammer-fantasy","aliases":["Warhammer Fantasy Battle","WHFB","Old World Warhammer"],"wikipedia_url":null,"image_url":null,"image_source":null,"image_credit":null,"image_license":null,"image_usage":null,"image_alt":null},"connections":[],"rabbit_holes":[],"copyright":{"theme":"warhammer-fantasy","title":"Warhammer Fantasy is not owned by Ton-o-Lore.","body":"Warhammer Fantasy, its characters, artwork, logos, and related intellectual property are the property of their respective rights holders, including Games Workshop Limited and other credited rights holders. Ton-o-Lore is an independent, unofficial fan and informational project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by those rights holders. This subject covers the classic Old World setting, not Warhammer 40,000 or Age of Sigmar. Identification logos and thumbnails, when shown, are low-resolution images used under a fair-use rationale for commentary and identification only — not free or redistributable artwork."},"subject":{"id":"warhammer-fantasy","name":"Warhammer Fantasy","theme":"warhammer-fantasy","path":"/warhammer-fantasy","logo":{"license":"fair_use","usage":"fair_use_identification","url":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/warhammerfb/images/2/2e/Warhammer_logo.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/360","alt":"Warhammer Fantasy logo","source":"https://warhammerfantasy.fandom.com/","credit":"Fair-use identification logo via Warhammer Fantasy Fandom. © Games Workshop."},"categories":["tabletop"]}}